! Trigonal selenium with spin-orbit coupling, for the harmonic routes' spinor checks.
!
! The one committed norm-conserving fully-relativistic dataset that makes an
! insulating crystal: SG15's `Se.rel-pbe-nc-sg15`. Trigonal Se is a chiral
! semiconductor, three atoms on helical chains along c (P3_121, x = 0.2254 at
! the experimental a = 4.366 A and c = 4.954 A), with no inversion centre, so
! every order of the current is nonzero, the second included; the spin-orbit
! coupling sits in the 2x2 `dvan_so` and nowhere else, which is what a spinor
! route has to carry beyond the scalar one.
!
! `ecutwfc = 20` is far from converged for SG15 selenium (about 40 Ry is) and is
! chosen for identities, which hold at any cutoff; `nosym`/`noinv` and an
! unshifted grid, for the polar tensors' sake (P24).
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    prefix = 'se'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 4, celldm(1) = 8.2509, celldm(3) = 1.1345,
    nat = 3, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 20.0,
    noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true.,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.,
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.5
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Se 78.97 Se.rel-pbe-nc-sg15.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 Se  0.2254  0.0000  0.333333333
 Se  0.0000  0.2254  0.666666667
 Se -0.2254 -0.2254  0.000000000
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 2 0 0 0
